{"reference":"1 Samuel 11","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":11,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Larger Story","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter belongs to the larger movement of First Samuel: the story moves from Eli’s failing priestly house through Samuel’s prophetic leadership, then follows Saul’s kingship and rejection before turning to David’s anointing, rise, exile, and Saul’s death. Saul’s deliverance of Jabesh-gilead is therefore one part of the book’s developing account of his reign.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 1","1 Samuel 10:1-27","1 Samuel 12:1-25","1 Samuel 13:1-23","1 Samuel 14:1-52","1 Samuel 15:1-35","1 Samuel 16:1-23","1 Samuel 17:1-58","1 Samuel 18:1-30","1 Samuel 19:1-24","1 Samuel 20:1-42","1 Samuel 21:1-15","1 Samuel 22:1-23","1 Samuel 23:1-29","1 Samuel 24:1-22","1 Samuel 25:1-44","1 Samuel 26:1-25","1 Samuel 27:1-12","1 Samuel 28:1-25","1 Samuel 29:1-11","1 Samuel 2:1-36","1 Samuel 30:1-31","1 Samuel 31:1-13","1 Samuel 3:1-21","1 Samuel 4:1-22","1 Samuel 5:1-12","1 Samuel 6:1-21","1 Samuel 7:1-17","1 Samuel 8:1-22","1 Samuel 9:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_011_808d8946b90be7b8a7442ea0"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}